          "path": "_m/d/4/c/j/placencia-wk/sanderling-belize-5678125655.jpg",
          "filename": "Sanderling, Belize (5678125655).jpg",
          "caption": "This is from my trip to Belize in 2005. This is a Sanderling aka Calidris alba, or Crocethia alba, or Erolia alba. (Thanks for Mr &amp; Mrs Apeteryx australis for pointing it out). It lives in the arctic, and was on vacation in Belize, just like we were!\nThis was a lucky shot with the 100-400mm telephoto on max. You can see the very narrow field of focus, and the bird is spot on. I remember struggling to point the heavy lens on these little birds that move all the time.\nISO 100, 400mm, f10, 1/500.\n\nProcessed in Adobe Camera Raw to brighten the exposure, add a bit of curves. Imagenomic Noiseware to clean the noise on the water, and a bit of smart sharpen on the bird.",
          "alt": "This is from my trip to Belize in 2005. This is a Sanderling aka Calidris alba, or Crocethia alba, or Erolia alba. (Thanks for Mr &amp; Mrs Apeteryx australis for pointing it out). It lives in the arctic, and was on vacation in Belize, just like we were!\nThis was a lucky shot with the 100-400mm telephoto on max. You can see the very narrow field of focus, and the bird is spot on. I remember struggling to point the heavy lens on these little birds that move all the time.\nISO 100, 400mm, f10, 1/500.\n\nProcessed in Adobe Camera Raw to brighten the exposure, add a bit of curves. Imagenomic Noiseware to clean the noise on the water, and a bit of smart sharpen on the bird.",
          "width": 2767,
          "height": 1844,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Pedro Szekely from Los Angeles, USA",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sanderling,_Belize_(5678125655).jpg",
